===== v16 dbb22ef diff on v_regfile_xfer.hpp =====
commit dbb22efb68f3d2539482eb823227a943e98dea17
Author: Nick Hung <nick@andestech.com>
Date:   Wed Jul 8 06:10:33 2026 +0800

    feat(hybrid): M-ext CSR block transport (ABI v4)

    Pin the shared ABI at v4, which appends struct hybrid_m_ext_csr -- the 51
    writable M-mode extension CSRs of HYBRID_M_EXT_CSR_LIST -- after the v3
    Andes block and bumps HYBRID_STATE_VERSION to 4. The block moves through
    the same capability-gated abstract-command loop as the v3 Andes CSRs:
    ResumeDriver restores and StateDrain re-reads each CSR one abstract access
    at a time, gated by caps.supports_csr() so a CSR the target core does not
    implement is never touched. Both sides now share the restore_andes_m_ext /
    drain_andes_m_ext helpers plus the new for_each_transport_csr walker in
    v_regfile_xfer.hpp, which iterates the Andes scalars, PMA, and M-ext blocks
    in one canonical order so every consumer stays in lockstep with the two
    X-macro lists. supported_andes_csr_names also emits the M-ext names, so
    --describe and the driver's --verify gate cover the new block through the
    address->gate map (UMODE..TRIGGER) the caps layer already carries. On an
